q q BT 9.6 TL/F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 284.9618 22.67717 Tm (Page 1)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 770.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 23 TL/F2 19 Tf 1 0 0 1 43.59146 4 Tm <4a4156412050524f4752414d4d494e472096204558504c41494e4544204e4f544553>Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 748.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14 TL/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 93.02846 4 Tm (Unit-wise theory + practical examples based on the provided syllabus)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 714.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 18 TL/F2 14 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 4 Tm T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 665.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT -.130681 Tw 14 TL/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.5 Tm T* 0 Tw T* T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 635.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 18 TL/F2 14 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 4 Tm <554e4954204920962042617369632053796e746163746963616c20436f6e7374727563747320696e204a617661>Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 586.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14 TL/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.5 Tm (This unit establishes the object-oriented foundation of Java. The important idea is that Java programs are organized)Tj T* (around classes and objects, and the language provides features such as encapsulation, method overloading, arrays,)Tj T* (strings and access control.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 563.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 15 TL/F2 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3.5 Tm (1. Java Platform and Program Structure)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 515.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14 TL/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.5 Tm (Java source code is compiled into bytecode. The Java Virtual Machine \(JVM\) executes this bytecode, which is why)Tj T* (the same compiled program can run on different operating systems when a compatible JVM is available. The JDK)Tj T* (provides development tools, the JRE provides the runtime environment, and the JVM performs bytecode execution.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 460.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 10 TL/F3 7.8 Tf 1 0 0 1 8 42.2 Tm (class Demo {)Tj T* (    void show\(\) {)Tj T* (        System.out.println\("Java program"\);)Tj T* (    })Tj T* (})Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 437.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 15 TL/F2 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3.5 Tm (2. Class, Object and Members)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 389.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14 TL/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.5 Tm (A class is a blueprint containing data and behavior. An object is a runtime instance of a class. Methods define)Tj T* (behavior, while fields represent the state of an object. Creating objects with new allocates an object and invokes its)Tj T* (constructor.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 274.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 10 TL/F3 7.8 Tf 1 0 0 1 8 102.2 Tm (class Student {)Tj T* (    String name;)Tj T* T* (    void display\(\) {)Tj T* (        System.out.println\(name\);)Tj T* (    })Tj T* (})Tj T* T* (Student s = new Student\(\);)Tj T* (s.name = "Amit";)Tj T* (s.display\(\);)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 251.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 15 TL/F2 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3.5 Tm (3. Tokens and Expressions)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 189.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14 TL/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 46.5 Tm (Java programs are formed from tokens such as keywords, identifiers, literals, operators and separators. Expressions)Tj T* -.117291 Tw (combine values and operators to produce a result. Operators include arithmetic, relational, logical, assignment, unary,)Tj T* 0 Tw (conditional and bitwise operators. Type casting converts a value from one type to another when the conversion is)Tj T* (permitted.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 124.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 10 TL/F3 7.8 Tf 1 0 0 1 8 52.2 Tm (int a = 10;)Tj T* (double b = 3.5;)Tj T* (double result = a + b;)Tj T* T* (int x = \(int\) b;       // explicit casting)Tj T* (boolean ok = a > 5 && b < 5;)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 101.3701 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 15 TL/F2 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 3.5 Tm (4. Decision and Looping)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 51.35433 53.37008 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14 TL/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.5 Tm (Control flow determines which statements execute and how many times they execute. if/else is used for conditions,)Tj T* (switch is useful for multiple fixed choices, and for/while/do-while are used for repetition. break terminates a loop or)Tj T* (switch, while continue skips the current iteration.)Tj T* ET Q Q
